g a file than encoding the same music in separate parts, so its use is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"preferred in this situation if feasible. A regular staff is the standard default staff-type.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails\/kind","type":"topic","title":"MXLStaffDetails.Kind"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLStaffDetails","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff-details element is used to indicate different types of staves. The optional number attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies the staff number from top to bottom on the system, as with clef. The print-object attribute is used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to indicate when a staff is not printed in a part, usually in large scores where empty parts are omitted. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is yes by default. If print-spacing is yes while print-object is no, the score is printed in cutaway format"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where vertical space is left for the empty part."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails/staffKind":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails\/staffkind","abstract":[{"text":"The kind of staff, such as ossia, cue, editorial, regular, or